WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
A digital footprint is the information created, collected,

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:08.280
or exposed through online activity, accounts, connected devices, services, public records,

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.580
and technical infrastructure.

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:13.810
It includes obvious material such as a public profile and less visible traces such as

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:14.755
service logs,

00:00:14.755 --> 00:00:16.240
metadata, and indexed records.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.875
An active footprint comes from deliberate sharing: posts, comments, uploads, resumes,

00:00:20.875 --> 00:00:22.335
websites, or public code.

00:00:22.335 --> 00:00:25.930
A passive footprint is collected or exposed as activity occurs,

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.205
sometimes without a clear publishing decision.

00:00:28.205 --> 00:00:31.520
Examples include tracking records, technical logs, search indexes,

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.050
and data held by third parties.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.555
Footprints can be personal, professional, organizational, or technical.

00:00:36.555 --> 00:00:38.870
A professional profile may reveal work history.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:43.445
An organization may expose domains, job postings, documents, and partners.

00:00:43.445 --> 00:00:47.190
Technical systems leave observable records such as certificates, public services,

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.700
and software characteristics.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:52.595
These traces matter because they affect privacy, security, safety, reputation,

00:00:52.595 --> 00:00:53.700
and investigations.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.125
One detail may seem harmless,

00:00:55.125 --> 00:00:58.480
but several accurate details can combine into a sensitive picture.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.880
Old or incorrect information can also create risk when it is treated as current fact.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.180
Legitimate defensive analysis can identify unnecessary exposure,

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:10.955
support incident response, verify organizational assets, and improve privacy controls.

00:01:10.955 --> 00:01:14.080
It should be bounded by purpose, authority, proportionality,

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.300
and respect for people affected by the information.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:19.825
A digital footprint is not a complete identity or a guaranteed truth.

00:01:19.825 --> 00:01:23.965
It is a changing set of observable traces that must be interpreted in context.

00:01:23.965 --> 00:01:27.100
Responsible work validates sources, minimizes personal data,

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.480
and uses findings to reduce risk rather than exploit individuals.
